findings.body:
`get_plan_bulk` now writes `results[tenant_id] = None` when validation fails. The new unit test and its name say the invalid tenant should be skipped, and the test asserts `len(result) == 2` and `"tenant-invalid" not in result`. Both assertions fail, because the result has three keys and `tenant-invalid` maps to `None`. The return annotation `dict[str, SubscriptionPlan]` is also violated.

::diff{file="api/services/billing_service.py" lines="284-292"}

::callout{type="warning"}
The test was written for "skip" behavior and the code implements "store None". One of them has to change. Skipping is the safer contract because callers index into the result without checking for `None`.

::diff{file="api/tests/unit_tests/services/test_billing_service.py" lines="1316-1319"}

`get_plan_bulk_with_cache` does not filter `None` out of `bulk_plans`. Step 2 copies every entry into `tenant_plans` and `plans_to_cache`, then `json.dumps(None)` writes the string `"null"` to Redis with a 600s TTL.

Failure scenario: a billing response with one malformed plan for tenant `T` leads to `get_plan_bulk` returning `{T: None}`. The caller gets `{T: None}`, and `plan["plan"]` raises `TypeError`. Within the TTL, every batch that includes `T` reads `"null"`, fails validation, logs an exception, and refetches. The bad entry therefore persists for ten minutes and produces repeated error logs.

::diff{file="api/services/billing_service.py" lines="361-377"}

::callout{type="warning"}
`plans_to_cache` is a copy of `bulk_plans` with the same keys and values, so it adds nothing. Dropping it and writing only validated plans removes the duplicate path as well.

`SubscriptionPlan` is a `TypedDict`, and its values are plain `dict` objects at runtime. Defining `__str__` on the class body therefore does nothing for real instances. I confirmed this in a standalone Python 3.12 run: the instance is a `dict`, and `str()` prints the dict literal. Type checkers also reject method definitions in a TypedDict body, so this addition is also likely to be flagged by mypy.

::diff{file="api/services/billing_service.py" lines="22-30"}

If a readable form is needed for logs, format it at the call site or in a helper function. Nothing in this PR uses the new string form.
